  "validation_notes": [
    "Game source is frozen at the source commit. Later commits add documentation, a fixed-size timing fixture, rebuilt browser export and validation without modifying game code.",
    "The final balance sample uses fixed 55 ms native combat ticks and six deterministic purchase policies with eight seeds each per difficulty. These are design samples, not human win rates.",
    "Surviving wave 30 completes Expedition even if the last individual fight was lost; completion and fight wins are recorded separately.",
    "The issue 19 public save enters combat at 2.017 seconds. Repositioning the player army while retaining the enemy formation also passes.",
    "The integrated issue 16 and 17 fixtures pass on the packaged source. The pause-clock fixture fixes resolution to 800x600; a preliminary unbounded 4K run at roughly 5 FPS exceeded its short-clip timing window. Separate layout checks cover 800x600 through 5K.",
    "Fresh and upgraded browser starts reached visible setup with no console warnings/errors. Every IndexedDB store is preserved byte for byte, including isolated game-data and save sentinels.",
    "The existing public encyclopedia content is retained with version metadata updated in all six campaign/language indexes."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Linux packages were runtime-tested. Windows, macOS and Android were audited for source/resource integrity and packaging without target-OS runtime tests; macOS is unsigned.",
    "Browser checks cover visible setup, engine cache replacement, storage preservation and console errors, not a complete campaign playthrough.",
    "Audio decoding and dispatch were checked with the Dummy audio driver; no listening assessment is claimed.",
    "No physical input-device or live network-peer qualification is claimed. Co-op requires matching versions.",
    "Timing measurements are local observations on an RTX 3090. Balance simulations do not establish human difficulty or competitive parity."
  ],
  "deployment_verification": "Live asset hashes and browser startup must pass before the draft release is published; receipts are retained in the release workspace."
